        choices: ["Comparing two exam papers and keeping the better of the two papers each time", "Sorting a pile of cards by swapping neighbours that are out of order", "Tallying each ballot under its candidate, then reading the tallies", "Splitting a pile of papers in half again and again, then joining the halves"],
        answer: 2,
        explanation: 'Counting sort never compares two items with each other. It tallies each item by its value and reads the tallies back in order.',
