        'Make 1,000 random whole numbers between 0 and 100 with `Array.from({ length: 1000 }, (_, i) => (i * 7919) % 101)`. Sort them with `countingSort(values, 100)` and with merge sort or the built-in sort, and check the two results are the same.',
        'Add a counter to count steps in counting sort (one for each tally and one for each value written). Compare it with 1,000 times log2 1,000, about 10,000. Then try values up to 100,000 and write one sentence on what that does to the counts array.',
