          explanation: 'Without a comparator, sort compares the text of each value: "100" < "25" < "3" < "40" because it looks at the first characters 1, 2, 3 and 4. The first line is therefore 100 25 3 40. The comparator a - b then sorts numerically ascending, giving 3 25 40 100.',
